/-!
# A meromorphic section generating a module over a covering family trivializes it

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S`, let `ℒ` be an `𝒪_X`-module and let `t` be a
meromorphic section of `ℒ`. Suppose that `t` *generates* `ℒ` over each member of a family
`Y : I → X_étale` of étale charts covering `X`, in the sense of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.GeneratesOnChart`: over each `Y i` there is a compatible family of
sections of `ℒ` freely generating it over every chart over `Y i`, whose image in the meromorphic
sections is `t`. Then `ℒ` is trivial, and so its Picard class vanishes.

This is the last step of the proof of Stacks 0EPX, where the étale-local argument produces
generation over a covering family of trivializing charts and the conclusion wanted is that the
class of `ℒ` in `Pic(X)` is zero.

The step is not immediate, because
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_iso_unit_of_bijective_smul_of_coversTop` asks for a **global
section** of `ℒ` by which multiplication is bijective over the covering family, while
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.GeneratesOnChart` supplies a section over each member of the family
only — `t` itself is merely meromorphic. The missing descent is proved here: the chartwise
sections agree wherever two of them are both defined, so they are a compatible family of
elements on the objects of the covering family, and a sheaf of modules on a site has a unique
global section restricting to such a family.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eq_of_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul_eq`: over one chart, the
  section of `ℒ` presenting `t` as `1 ⊗ e` is unique among free generators.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul_of_hom`: such a
  presentation restricts to every chart over the chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eq_of_eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul`: hence two charts
  carrying such a presentation of the same `t` give the *same* section of `ℒ` over any chart
  lying over both.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_sections_of_generatesOnChart_coversTop`: a global section of
  `ℒ` which presents `t` and freely generates `ℒ` over every chart over a member of the covering
  family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.picardClass_eq_zero_of_generatesOnChart_coversTop`: therefore the
  Picard class of an invertible `ℒ` generated by a meromorphic section over a covering family is
  zero.

## Implementation notes

The uniqueness is the one place where anything is used about `𝒪_X ⟶ 𝒦_X`. Two free generators of
`ℒ` over a chart differ by a unit `v` of the regular functions there
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isUnit_smul_of_bijective_smul`), and moving that unit across the
tensor turns the two presentations into `1 ⊗ e` and `v · 1 ⊗ e`; a free generator reads the
meromorphic sections injectively
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.injective_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_tmul`), so the image of `v` in
`𝒦_X(V)` is `1`, and `𝒪_X(V) ⟶ 𝒦_X(V)` is injective
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.injective_toMeromorphicFunctionSheaf`) — which holds on any algebraic
space, with no integrality or affineness hypothesis. Hence `v = 1` and the two generators agree.

With uniqueness in hand the gluing is Mathlib's: the chartwise sections are a
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.FamilyOfElementsOnObjects` of the underlying presheaf of abelian groups
of `ℒ`, uniqueness makes it
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.FamilyOfElementsOnObjects.IsCompatible`, and
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.FamilyOfElementsOnObjects.IsCompatible.existsUnique_section` produces
the global section from the sheaf condition and
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.CoversTop`. The sections of the presheaf of modules are by
definition the sections of that presheaf of abelian groups, so no transport is needed.

Nothing here asks that `t` be a *regular* meromorphic section, nor that `X` be integral, decent
or locally Noetherian: generation over the covering family is the whole hypothesis, and
invertibility of `ℒ` enters only to have a Picard class to speak of.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EPX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EPX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite TensorProduct

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

attribute [local instance] pointTopology
attribute [local instance] chartMeromorphicAlgebra
attribute [local instance] meromorphicSectionModuleRingedSiteModule

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
variable {X : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)
variable (L : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X hX)

/-! ### The section presenting a meromorphic section over a chart is unique -/

include hX in
/-- **A free generator presenting a given meromorphic section is unique.** Let `e` restrict to a
free generator of `ℒ` over every chart over `V`, and let `m` be a free generator of `ℒ` over a
chart `W` over `V`. If `1 ⊗ e` and `1 ⊗ m` have the same image in the sheaf `𝒦_X(ℒ)` of
meromorphic sections over `W`, then `m` *is* the restriction of `e` to `W`.

The two generators differ by a unit `v` of `𝒪_X(W)`, which moves across the tensor onto the
coefficient; a free generator reads the meromorphic sections injectively, so the image of `v` in
`𝒦_X(W)` is `1`, and `𝒪_X(W) ⟶ 𝒦_X(W)` is injective. -/
theorem eq_of_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul_eq (V : SmallEtale B S hS X)
    (e : (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) → (W ⟶ V) → L.val.obj (op W))
    (hcompat : ∀ (W W' : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : W ⟶ V) (g : W' ⟶ W),
      (L.val.map g.op).hom (e W k) = e W' (g ≫ k))
    (hfree : ∀ (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : W ⟶ V),
      Function.Bijective fun r : chartRing B S hS X hX W ↦ r • e W k)
    (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : W ⟶ V) (m : L.val.obj (op W))
    (hm : Function.Bijective fun r : chartRing B S hS X hX W ↦ r • m)
    (h : toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L W
          ((1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
              (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op W))
            ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX W] e W k :
            (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op W)) =
        toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L W
          ((1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
              (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op W))
            ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX W] m :
            (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op W))) :
    e W k = m := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_isUnit_smul_of_bijective_smul B S hS X hX L W (e W k) m
    (hfree W k) hm
  have hid : e W (𝟙 W ≫ k) = e W k := congrArg (e W) (Category.id_comp k)
  have hinj := injective_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_tmul B S hS X hX L W
    (fun W' g ↦ e W' (g ≫ k))
    (fun W₁ W₂ g i ↦ (hcompat W₁ W₂ (g ≫ k) i).trans
      (congrArg (e W₂) (Category.assoc i g k).symm))
    (fun W₁ g ↦ hfree W₁ (g ≫ k))
  rw [hid] at hinj
  have hswap : ((1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
          (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op W))
        ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX W] m :
        (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op W)) =
      ((algebraMap (chartRing B S hS X hX W)
            ((meromorphicChartSheaf B S hS X hX).obj.obj (op W))
          (v : chartRing B S hS X hX W)) ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX W] e W k :
        (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op W)) := by
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z : L.val.obj (op W) ↦
      ((1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
          (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op W))
        ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX W] z :
        (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op W))) hv) ?_
    refine Eq.trans (meromorphicSectionModule_tmul_smul B S hS X hX L W
      (v : chartRing B S hS X hX W) 1 (e W k)) ?_
    exact congrArg (fun z : (meromorphicChartSheaf B S hS X hX).obj.obj (op W) ↦
      (z ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX W] e W k :
        (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op W)))
      (mul_one _)
  have h1 : (1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op W)) =
      algebraMap (chartRing B S hS X hX W)
        ((meromorphicChartSheaf B S hS X hX).obj.obj (op W)) (v : chartRing B S hS X hX W) :=
    hinj (h.trans (congrArg (toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L W) hswap))
  have h2 : (1 : chartRing B S hS X hX W) = (v : chartRing B S hS X hX W) :=
    injective_toMeromorphicFunctionSheaf B S hS X hX W
      (((toMeromorphicFunctionSheaf B S hS X hX).hom.app (op W)).hom.map_one.trans h1)
  rw [hv, ← h2, one_smul]

include hX in
/-- **The presentation of a meromorphic section as `1 ⊗ e` restricts to every chart over the
chart.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_tmul_restrict` at the coefficient
`1`, whose restriction is again `1`. -/
theorem eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul_of_hom
    (t : MeromorphicSection.{u, u} B S hS X hX L) (V : SmallEtale B S hS X)
    (e : (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) → (W ⟶ V) → L.val.obj (op W))
    (hcompat : ∀ (W W' : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : W ⟶ V) (g : W' ⟶ W),
      (L.val.map g.op).hom (e W k) = e W' (g ≫ k))
    (hpres : t.eval (op V) = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L V
      ((1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
          (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op V))
        ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX V] e V (𝟙 V) :
        (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op V)))
    (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : W ⟶ V) :
    t.eval (op W) = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L W
      ((1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
          (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op W))
        ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX W] e W k :
        (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op W)) := by
  rw [eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_tmul_restrict B S hS X hX L t V e hcompat
    (1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
      (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op V)) hpres W k, map_one]

include hX in
/-- **Two charts over which a meromorphic section generates a module give the same section of
that module.** If `t` is presented as `1 ⊗ e` over `V` and as `1 ⊗ e'` over `V'`, both families
being free generators over every chart over their chart, then over any chart `W` lying over both
the two sections of `ℒ` agree.

Both presentations restrict to `W`, where
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eq_of_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul_eq` identifies the two
generators. -/
theorem eq_of_eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul
    (t : MeromorphicSection.{u, u} B S hS X hX L) {V V' : SmallEtale B S hS X}
    (e : (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) → (W ⟶ V) → L.val.obj (op W))
    (hcompat : ∀ (W W' : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : W ⟶ V) (g : W' ⟶ W),
      (L.val.map g.op).hom (e W k) = e W' (g ≫ k))
    (hfree : ∀ (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : W ⟶ V),
      Function.Bijective fun r : chartRing B S hS X hX W ↦ r • e W k)
    (hpres : t.eval (op V) = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L V
      ((1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
          (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op V))
        ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX V] e V (𝟙 V) :
        (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op V)))
    (e' : (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) → (W ⟶ V') → L.val.obj (op W))
    (hcompat' : ∀ (W W' : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : W ⟶ V') (g : W' ⟶ W),
      (L.val.map g.op).hom (e' W k) = e' W' (g ≫ k))
    (hfree' : ∀ (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : W ⟶ V'),
      Function.Bijective fun r : chartRing B S hS X hX W ↦ r • e' W k)
    (hpres' : t.eval (op V') = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L V'
      ((1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
          (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op V'))
        ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX V'] e' V' (𝟙 V') :
        (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op V')))
    (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : W ⟶ V) (k' : W ⟶ V') :
    e W k = e' W k' :=
  eq_of_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul_eq B S hS hX L V e hcompat hfree W k (e' W k')
    (hfree' W k')
    ((eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul_of_hom B S hS hX L t V e hcompat
        hpres W k).symm.trans
      (eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul_of_hom B S hS hX L t V' e' hcompat'
        hpres' W k'))

/-! ### The global section, and the vanishing of the Picard class -/

include hX in
/-- **A meromorphic section generating a module over a covering family comes from a global
section.** If `t` generates `ℒ` over every member of a family `Y` of étale charts covering `X`,
then there is a global section `m` of `ℒ` which over every chart `W` lying over a member of `Y`
freely generates `ℒ` and presents `t` as `1 ⊗ m`.

The sections supplied over the members of `Y` agree wherever two of them are defined
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eq_of_eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul`), so they are a
compatible family of elements on the objects of `Y`, and a sheaf has a unique global section
restricting to such a family. -/
theorem exists_sections_of_generatesOnChart_coversTop
    (t : MeromorphicSection.{u, u} B S hS X hX L)
    {I : Type*} (Y : I → SmallEtale B S hS X)
    (hY : (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X).CoversTop Y)
    (hgen : ∀ i, GeneratesOnChart B S hS hX L t (Y i)) :
    ∃ m : L.val.sections, ∀ (i : I) (W : SmallEtale B S hS X), (W ⟶ Y i) →
      (Function.Bijective fun r : chartRing B S hS X hX W ↦ r • m.eval (op W)) ∧
        t.eval (op W) = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L W
          ((1 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
              (meromorphicRingedSite B S hS X hX).O).obj.obj (op W))
            ⊗ₜ[chartRing B S hS X hX W] m.eval (op W) :
            (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op W)) := by
  classical
  choose e hc hb hp using hgen
  have hwd : ∀ (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) (i j : I) (k : W ⟶ Y i) (k' : W ⟶ Y j),
      e i W k = e j W k' := fun W i j k k' ↦
    eq_of_eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul B S hS hX L t (e i) (hc i) (hb i) (hp i)
      (e j) (hc j) (hb j) (hp j) W k k'
  have hLsheaf : Presheaf.IsSheaf (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X)
      (L.val.presheaf ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :=
    GrothendieckTopology.HasSheafCompose.isSheaf _ L.isSheaf
  have hkey : ∀ (Z : SmallEtale B S hS X) (i j : I) (f : Z ⟶ Y i) (g : Z ⟶ Y j),
      (L.val.map f.op).hom (e i (Y i) (𝟙 (Y i))) =
        (L.val.map g.op).hom (e j (Y j) (𝟙 (Y j))) := by
    intro Z i j f g
    rw [hc i (Y i) Z (𝟙 (Y i)) f, hc j (Y j) Z (𝟙 (Y j)) g]
    exact hwd Z i j _ _
  have hcomp : Presheaf.FamilyOfElementsOnObjects.IsCompatible
      (F := L.val.presheaf ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat.{u}) (Y := Y)
      fun i ↦ e i (Y i) (𝟙 (Y i)) := fun Z i j f g ↦ hkey Z i j f g
  obtain ⟨m, hm, -⟩ := hcomp.existsUnique_section hY hLsheaf
  refine ⟨m, fun i W k ↦ ?_⟩
  have hmW : PresheafOfModules.sections.eval m (op W) = e i W k := by
    have hsec : (L.val.map k.op).hom (m.1 (op (Y i))) = m.1 (op W) := m.2 k.op
    show m.1 (op W) = e i W k
    rw [← hsec, hm i, hc i (Y i) W (𝟙 (Y i)) k, Category.comp_id]
  rw [hmW]
  exact ⟨hb i W k, eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_one_tmul_of_hom B S hS hX L t (Y i)
    (e i) (hc i) (hp i) W k⟩

include hX in
/-- **A meromorphic section generating an invertible module over a covering family trivializes
it.** The Picard class of an invertible `𝒪_X`-module `ℒ` is zero as soon as some meromorphic
section of `ℒ` generates it over each member of a family of étale charts covering `X`.

This is the last step of the proof of Stacks 0EPX. The global section of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_sections_of_generatesOnChart_coversTop` is the one
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_iso_unit_of_bijective_smul_of_coversTop` asks for, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.picardClass_eq_zero_iff` turns the resulting isomorphism `ℒ ≅ 𝒪_X` into
the vanishing of the class. -/
theorem picardClass_eq_zero_of_generatesOnChart_coversTop
    (hL : IsInvertibleModule (B := B) ⟨X, hX⟩ L)
    (t : MeromorphicSection.{u, u} B S hS X hX L)
    {I : Type*} (Y : I → SmallEtale B S hS X)
    (hY : (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X).CoversTop Y)
    (hgen : ∀ i, GeneratesOnChart B S hS hX L t (Y i)) :
    picardClass (B := B) ⟨X, hX⟩ L hL = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_sections_of_generatesOnChart_coversTop B S hS hX L t Y hY hgen
  refine (picardClass_eq_zero_iff (B := B) ⟨X, hX⟩ L hL).2 ?_
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_iso_unit_of_bijective_smul_of_coversTop L m Y hY
    fun i W k ↦ (hm i W k).1

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
